=== PARITY (vs web QuickNavWidget.tsx → QuickNav.tsx) ===
  Composition -> QuickNavWidget.tsx renders <WidgetShell noPadding><QuickNav/></WidgetShell> with NO
    title → the native surface is likewise header-less: just the padded shortcut grid inside the widget's
    own glass card (sibling-widget convention). QuickNav.tsx maps a static NAV_ITEMS[4] into a
    `grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3` of GlassPanel links → native LazyVGrid (2 cols narrow / 4 cols
    full-width via QuickNavLayout) of QuickNavTile (tinted icon square + label + description + chevron).
  Catalog -> the 4 destinations reproduce NAV_ITEMS verbatim:
    Drives  (nav.drives/nav.drivesDesc, "Trip history",        #00f0ff) -> /driving
    Charging(nav.charging/nav.chargingDesc,"Sessions & costs",  #10b981) -> /charging
    Analytics(nav.analytics/…Desc, "Fleet insights",           #a855f7) -> /analytics
    Battery (nav.battery/nav.batteryDesc,"Health & degradation",#f59e0b) -> /energy
    Order preserved (CaseIterable). Accent colors are the exact web hex (verified by test).
  Icons -> web lucide Route/BatteryCharging/Gauge/Activity → SF Symbols
    point.topleft.down.to.point.bottomright.curvepath / battery.100.bolt / gauge.medium /
    waveform.path.ecg (+ chevron.right). All confirmed present on the toolchain (AppKit probe).
  Routing -> web <Link to="/drives|/charging|/analytics|/battery"> → delegated to the host via an injected
    `onNavigate(QuickNavDestination)` seam (the view performs no navigation itself), carrying the native
    canonical route path resolved by AppRouteParser (/drives→/driving, /battery→/energy alias). webPath +
    routePath both asserted in tests.
  i18n -> useTranslation('dashboard') t('nav.X', default) → QuickNavStrings table "QuickNavWidget"; the 8
    web nav.* keys carry the exact web English defaults. No hardcoded literals in the view.
  Data -> web "Data sources: (none)". QuickNav has NO query/hook; the production StaticQuickNavSource
    publishes the catalog (native analogue of the NAV_ITEMS module constant) through the P1/S8 seam.

=== STATES (every state renders) ===
  content  -> the responsive shortcut grid (the real, always-on web state).
  loading  -> skeleton grid (defensive framework state; web shell Skeleton intent).
  empty    -> ContentUnavailableView "No shortcuts" (defensive — catalog resolved empty).
  error    -> icon + title + Retry (defensive — catalog failed; web QueryError intent).
  stale/offline -> N/A and intentionally NOT fabricated. The web source is purely presentational with
    NO data fetch and NO network/freshness dimension (no query, no LiveConnectionState), and the
    shortcuts are local routes that work offline by nature. Rendering a "Live/Stale/Offline" chip would
    imply live data that does not exist (silent drift). This is faithful reproduction of the source, not
    scope-narrowing — there is no stale/offline branch in QuickNav to port. All four reachable phases are
    snapshot-rendered green below.

